course: dictionary
lesson: 4622
title: Highway: a big main road
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change a little depending on where you live. «Highway» is one of them. In the USA and Canada, people use it for a big main road, the kind where cars go fast. In the UK, people more often say «motorway» or «main road». Context clues help you see which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the words around it: «The Highway Code gives a stopping distance at 30 mph of about 23 m.» The Highway Code is a book of road rules, so highway here is about roads and safety. The sentence tells you what the word means, even if you have never seen it before.
explain: Some phrases use highway in a special way. «My way or the highway» means do it my way or go, said by someone who won't bend. This is an idiom, so you cannot work out its meaning from each word alone. The sentence around it is your clue.
explain: Toad, in a famous old story, loves «the open road, the dusty highway, the heath, the common». The list tells you that a highway is a road you travel along, like the other places he enjoys.
fact: A highway is a main road, usually big and fast, that joins towns and cities.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «highway» is the everyday word for a big main road, like a «freeway» or «interstate».
fact: In the UK, the Highway Code is the book of road rules, and it advises cyclists to wear a helmet.
fact: Old or formal use: highway can mean any public road.
fact: Never walk or play on a highway, because the cars travel too fast to stop quickly.
exercise: «The Highway Code gives a stopping distance at 30 mph of about 23 m.» What is the Highway Code? | A map of the stars | A kind of car | *A book of road rules
exercise: An American says, «Take the highway into town.» What does highway mean here? | A school playground | A tiny footpath through the woods | *A big main road | A river bank
exercise: «My way or the highway» is said by someone who won't bend. What does it mean? | Walk along the highway with me | Stop and listen to everyone's ideas | *Do it my way or go | Drive more slowly
test: Why should you never play on a highway? | Highways are too short for games | It is against the rules of football | Highways are made of soft grass | *Cars travel fast and it is very dangerous
test: The Highway Code says cyclists should do what? | Carry a ladder | *Wear a helmet | Ride with their eyes shut | Sing loudly while they ride
exam: Which phrase is an idiom meaning «do it my way or go»? | The Highway Code | Highway patrol | On the highway | *My way or the highway
